  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VU-Sexual Violence prevention</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this initiative, the Center for Legal Advice &#x2013; Vinh University (VU) desires to address the issue of sexual abuse, targeting the children of ethnicity in Thanh Chuong district and several communes in Do Luong district, Nghe An. The project aims to raise legal awareness for children, especially girls from 10 to 16 years old through communication and dissemination of laws on preventing the risk of sexual abuse. Simultaneously, it emphasizes the importance of raising awareness for child caretakers (parents, grandparents, and relatives) about knowledge of child sexual abuse prevention and control. Especially, to protect abused children in the locality, the Center will develop key including staff of the Women&apos;s Union, commune medical stations, commune judicial officers, commune and district police officers, middle school teachers, etc. elementary school and primary school, village elder, village head, Ho Chi MinhCommunist Youth Union cadre, parents or caregivers... and equipped with knowledge, legal communication skills and  legal consultancy skills, legal aid on the protection of children&apos;s rights. Furthermore, the Center aims to provide legal advice, initial legal aid for cases of children being sexually abused or at risk of being sexually abused. Last but not least, to ensure children&#x2019;s rights to be protected, the project also targets to recommend policies and coordinate to develop regulations and plans for coordination in between the agencies with authority in Thanh Chuong and Do Luong districts in receiving and explaining in the receipt and settlement ofdenunciations and news reports about crimes, propose prosecution, investigate and conduct instance trial for cases of child sexual abuse. The expected results are to be: raising legal knowledge and understanding for 3500 (1500 women, 600 ethnics, 3000 children, 500 poor/near-poor people), providing legal aids and consultation for 120 cases, develop 1 research for policy recommendations for local authorities on children rights protection.</narrative>
  </description>
